Investigation evidence chain — SideCamera AC-4 timing — revision 2

Scope: reproduced single-camera AC-4 cadence failure only. The accepted five-minute capture remains the reproduction. Each numbered item is an observation with its source time and capture path; the concluding mechanism is inference, not another observed link. PTS semantics are V4L2 ts-src-soe (start of exposure), not EOF.

1. Observed — accepted current-source five-minute reproduction (2026-11-15 08:15:26–08:20:31 UTC). The preserved executed log records 6,050 matched frames over 302.506666 s, 6,049 EOF intervals, mean 49.998692 ms (20.000523 fps), maximum 89.163715 ms, and 753 intervals above 60 ms. The failure is still a max-gap failure; the capture is reused and was not rerun for revision 2. Investigation `evidence/reproduction.log` is byte-identical to `../build/evidence/runtime-smoke-ac4-r2.2-round2.log`, SHA-256 `de804d35326c6925862d2c8b36708d4a14a10b05120076924f523397976e8c55`. The build probe/reports retain source lineage; `system/sidecamerad.py` was SHA-256 `494fb8b88fda8bcf1d8301225019f4f01f4b77a0bb5cb3e69dde47ed96e1309b`, unchanged through later diagnostics.

2. Observed — same-run FFmpeg PTS/read capture (created 2026-11-15 09:55:44 UTC). It records 600 output-order PTS/read pairs and no payload bytes. PTS are in the monotonic domain and source-tagged ts-src-soe. After the initial startup interval, 598 PTS intervals averaged 50.006737 ms, maxed at 52.128 ms, and had zero >60 ms. Over the same steady interval window, raw-frame read completions had 89 intervals >60 ms and a maximum of 89.946 ms. Sources: `../build/reports/report_pts-read-correlation-r2.3-r1.md` SHA-256 `969228a65ddd220b407f19be0e0b6301be0c02f9e2e90909beac9f4722ee20a3`; `../build/artifacts/pts-read-correlation-r2.3-r1.json` SHA-256 `067a4b4d3dee1d3d836490dcaa489d393ae916bda52ebb101da5fcde0c822bba`; showinfo capture `../build/evidence/ffmpeg-showinfo-pts-read-correlation-r2.3-r1.log` SHA-256 `848d42a5562f3145222130badeeda8e477a187b0959f614d135b3dcf4a90e183`.

3. Observed — corrected same-run V4L2 DQBUF / PTS / output-write / full-read correlation (created 2026-11-15 10:00:10 UTC). After startup, 600 DQBUF intervals averaged 49.994824 ms, max 58.634 ms, with zero >60 ms; 598 SOE PTS intervals averaged 50.006737 ms, max 52.128 ms, with zero >60 ms. The 598 raw-output write-boundary intervals averaged 49.957065 ms, max 89.580 ms, with 146 >60 ms. The 598 Python full-read completion intervals averaged 49.957056 ms, max 89.587 ms, with 147 >60 ms. Write-start to full-read completion was median 0.116 ms, p95 0.196 ms. This comparison places the observed cadence divergence after the DQBUF timestamps and before raw-pipe delivery, without proving exact frame identity: there were 602 successful DQBUF calls for 600 outputs, and the raw ioctl trace omitted V4L2 sequence fields. Sources: `../build/reports/report_dqbuf-output-correlation-r2.3-r1.md` SHA-256 `6d96162d197305e68eb88c8ae29cd8f67f957930c627ce01d4d8932318336c5a`; `../build/artifacts/dqbuf-output-correlation-r2.3-r1.json` SHA-256 `29c587a2bf121c8e35c16481400f621686505cf3ad3afe0f95cb7f0ffab130b2`; corrected raw trace `../build/evidence/v4l2-dqbuf-ffmpeg-output-r2.3-r1.strace` SHA-256 `5eb1ed5f3f73c01d88e6745a2c4c7df170f9d0324319ac374c1f4a84b98fd1b5`.

4. Observed — corrected DQBUF trace output write durations. Across 25,800 writes on the FFmpeg raw output descriptor, duration was median 0.058 ms, p95 0.153 ms, p99 0.256 ms, maximum 10.554 ms; none exceeded 50 ms. This does not support sustained pipe backpressure as the main source of long output gaps. Separate writes-only trace capture (created 2026-11-15 09:48:31 UTC) also found write-boundary and read-completion intervals closely aligned, but that trace was straced, had observer overhead, and was not paired with the DQBUF capture; retain it as corroboration only. Sources: corrected raw trace above and `../build/reports/report_ffmpeg-stdout-write-trace-r2.3-r1.md` SHA-256 `c0b6822692ce075774854ddcba5996d32e633382659e5767e00efe25fe6a1268`; writes-only raw trace `../build/evidence/ffmpeg-stdout-write-trace-r2.3-r1.strace` SHA-256 `9878b91cb3fde20172cd524c399a7220f245ee2c6c3561f2e567bf30143a9cc4`.

5. Observed — untraced 600-frame FFmpeg capture with per-thread `/proc/<pid>/task/*/schedstat` snapshots (created 2026-11-15 10:20:43 UTC). It completed 600/600 frames and recorded 599 read intervals: mean 49.992047 ms, median 50.341057 ms, p95 64.946614 ms, p99 73.227160 ms, maximum 80.383947 ms; 77 intervals exceeded 60 ms. Scheduler counters were available for `ffmpeg`, `dec0:0:mjpeg`, `dmx0:video4linu`, and `mux0:rawvideo`. On the 77 long intervals, summed runqueue delay averaged 1.469 ms, mean maximum single-thread delay was 0.988 ms, and 3/77 had any thread wait >=5 ms; the maximum summed delay was 10.868 ms. On the other 522 intervals, the respective means were 1.273 ms and 0.848 ms, and 13/522 had any thread wait >=5 ms. The probe read 829,440,000 bytes, saved no image payload, returned 0, reaped the child, and observed no source hash drift. Full raw capture: `artifacts/ffmpeg-schedstat-600-r2.json` SHA-256 `e3bea2a7874fdb5e6b98d6aeb7fbaeca65308845feb684883d8491e11b01aa36`; concise capture log: `ffmpeg-schedstat-600-r2.log` SHA-256 `971a7fc09d7766f30aba668ce1ecc2ea38d2dc687c2359a458abb24fbcaadc2b`.

Inference (medium confidence): cadence jitter appears after V4L2 buffer dequeue and inside FFmpeg processing/output before raw-pipe delivery. The close write-boundary/read-completion cadence and sub-millisecond write-to-read lag do not support a separate Python reader backlog. Scheduler-delay deltas do not support CPU runqueue scheduling as the primary cause, and the short write syscall durations do not support sustained pipe backpressure. The remaining boundary is FFmpeg internal processing/output pacing or synchronization: exact decode/filter/output wait and writer-thread attribution were not isolated. DQBUF-to-output frame identity is also unproven because sequence fields were absent and counts differ.

Timestamp disposition: retain `timestampEof` as host-monotonic time sampled after each complete raw NV12 frame read. The FFmpeg PTS are V4L2 SOE timestamps, not EOF; do not substitute them for `timestampEof`. No source edit or five-minute capture rerun occurred during this revision.
